        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-18T18:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, I we reboot, we reinitialize the pmp entries. \n\nThe current zephyr upstream [z_riscv_pmp_init](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/arch/riscv/core/pmp.c;l\u003d593?q\u003dpmp.c\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d592-,593,-594) can allow either locked global entries or unlocked global entries configured by `CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL`. If we still need to `sysjump` from RO to RW, our best option is to use the `CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL`.",
      "parentUuid": "3ddb264d_d96c9bff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "a5ace05f2580d38a5246f210a0ee821fd72c4e00",
