      "writtenOn": "2025-12-18T22:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The current zephyr upstream z_riscv_pmp_init can allow either locked global entries or unlocked global entries configured by CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL. If we still need to sysjump from RO to RW, our best option is to use the CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL.\n\nYou could set `CONFIG_PMP_NO_LOCK_GLOBAL` and then lock them ourselves, right?",
